<title>JAPAN: Bangchak awards two Oman in July tender-traders.</title>
<headline>Bangchak awards two Oman in July tender-traders.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's Bangchak Petroleum Plc awarded at least two Oman cargoes and one Murban cargo in its tender to buy July-loading crude oil, traders said on Friday.</p>
<p>The two Oman cargoes were awarded to a Japanese trading company at Dubai quotes plus 60 cents.</p>
<p>The 500,000 barrel Murban was thought to have been sold by a second Japanese trading company at a discount of 33.5 cents to the official selling price.</p>
<p>There were also vague reports that a U.S. major may have sold an Oman cargo to Bangchak, but the details were unavailable.</p>
<p>The details of the awards could not be immediately confirmed with the companies concerned.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Energy Desk +81-3-5473-3706</p>
</text>
